From f3e83c03a52e6b904e190be012e1e44e3978fee2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aniket Randive <arandive@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2025 19:21:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] i2c: qcom-geni: Add asynchronous read support for CCU QUP

Add asynchronous I2C read support for CCU QUP controllers. This enables
static memory allocation for up to four async frames per sync channel,
with bitmap-based usage tracking. For each async read frame, dedicated
buffer pointers are maintained, and data is copied back to user space
after the transfer completes. Since memory is now persistent, the
previous logic for releasing frames has been removed.

Additionally, this patch enhances resource usage by dynamically
allocate the main CCU QUP structure to reduce memory overhead on
platforms without CCU QUP support. It also disallows asynchronous
transfers on regular GPII channels and avoids dynamic memory
allocations for CCU synchronous writes and extract frame configuration.

Also fixes a potential NULL dereference in QUP_NOTIF_EV_TYPE handling.
The driver attempted to access gchan without acquiring it. Ensure the
gchan pointer is retrieved before dereferencing.

Change-Id: I71c44150e3a3f0a1914d331da6a10fa1119bcc9b
Signed-off-by: Maramaina Naresh <mnaresh@qti.qualcomm.com>
